   "prompt": "In the expression ⁿ√36, the value n is called the:",
   "choices": [
    "radicand",
    "index",
    "principal root",
    "coefficient"
   ],
   "answer": "B",
   "explanation": "The index is the small number in the crook of the radical that tells you which root to take. 36 is the radicand."
  },
  {
   "type": "mcq",
   "prompt": "Simplify ∛(343a¹⁸b⁶).",
   "choices": [
    "7a⁶b²",
    "7a⁵b³",
    "49a⁶b²",
    "7|a⁶b²|"
   ],
   "answer": "A",
   "explanation": "343a¹⁸b⁶ = (7a⁶b²)³. The index is odd, so no absolute value is needed."
